  "final_text": "Both objects exist and are verified by reading them back from the API.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-d1bb6a4e Web logs overview`** (ID `32febdee-c9b0-4193-abc5-c3a3dd75de43`)\n- Four metric panels: Total requests (count), 5xx responses (count with KQL `response : \"503\"`), Average response size (average of `bytes`), and Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`).\n- Two line charts over time: all requests, and 5xx responses (ES|QL).\n- A pie chart of requests by `response.keyword`.\n- Time range is absolute, 2026-10-01 to 2026-12-31, so the panels show the sample data. A relative \"last 15 minutes\" default would show nothing.\n\n**Rule: `EFF-d1bb6a4e 5xx spike`** (ID `255a97c9-a242-454f-879a-51b360ed9c8f`)\n- Elasticsearch query rule (`.es-query`), DSL query filtering `response.keyword: \"503\"`.\n- Checks every 1m over a 5m window, fires when count `> 10`, grouped over all documents.\n- Enabled. Its last execution status is `ok`.\n- It has no actions attached, so it creates alerts but notifies no one. Tell me if you want a connector added.\n\n**Data findings**\n- 14,074 documents. Response codes are 200 (12,832), 404 (801), and 503 (441). The only 5xx code present is 503.\n- Timestamps run from 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, which is partly in the future relative to today (2026-10-12). The rule only counts documents whose timestamps fall in the last 5 minutes, so it may not fire until matching data arrives.\n\n**Not checked**\n- I did not render the dashboard in a browser. The panels passed the API's schema validation, but I have not visually confirmed the layout or the pie chart.",
